IMPORT prelude

-- National Servicemen (Employment) Act 1970 (Singapore) -- the register of persons who have completed full-time national service
-- (s 4), a Minister's order that employers hire only from the register (s 5), the Director's consent and the appeal against its
-- refusal (s 6), the registered person's duty to notify the Director (s 7), entry, information and summons powers and their offences
-- (ss 8, 9), and the liability of corporate officers (s 10).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/NSEA1970.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; its Legislative History lists only
-- Act 28 of 1970 and the 1970 and 1985 Revised Editions, so no amending Act is annotated. The Arrangement of Sections at the top of
-- the deposit is shifted by one line against the body; the section numbers here follow the body.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance to ordinary people in Singapore: it is the statute about securing jobs for men
-- who have finished full-time national service, and about the employers who hire them. SCOPED to nearly the whole Act, which is short.
-- Not encoded: the appointment of the Director and Assistant Directors (s 3), the form of the register (s 4(2)), the Minister's power
-- to vary or revoke an order (s 5(6)), the composition of the Appeals Board (s 6(3)), and the rule-making power (s 11). Whether any
-- order under s 5(1) is in force today is NOT in the deposit and is not assumed here.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `National Servicemen (Employment) Act 1970`

§§ `2 and 4 -- the register`

-- s 2: "'employee' includes any person seeking employment"; "'employer' includes any person desiring to employ other persons";
-- "'registered person' means a person whose name appears for the time being in the register".
-- s 4(1): "The Director shall establish and maintain a register of persons who have completed full-time national service under any
-- written law for the time being in force relating to national service or enlistment."
GIVEN `has completed full-time national service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `belongs on the register` IF `has completed full-time national service`

§§ `5(1)-(3) -- an order to hire only from the register`

-- s 5(1): the Minister may by Gazette order direct that an employer to whom the order applies "shall not, except with the written
-- consent of the Director, engage or re-engage any employee otherwise than from among registered persons".
-- (2): no order applies to an employer who takes into employment a person "whom apart from that subsection it would have been his duty
-- to take into employment either (a) by virtue of any written law; or (b) by virtue of any agreement made before 2 January 1971".
-- (3): an order may apply to all or specified employers, all or specified employees, and "may provide that any directions contained in
-- the order shall not apply in any specified circumstances".
DECLARE Hiring HAS
    `an order under section 5 is in force`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the order covers the employer`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the order covers this kind of employee`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the order excepts these circumstances`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer must take the person on by written law`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer must take the person on by a pre-1971 agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a registered person`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Director consented in writing`                      IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the hiring` IS A Hiring
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order applies to the hiring` IF
        `the hiring`'s `an order under section 5 is in force`
    AND `the hiring`'s `the order covers the employer`
    AND `the hiring`'s `the order covers this kind of employee`
    AND (NOT `the hiring`'s `the order excepts these circumstances`)
    AND (NOT `the hiring`'s `the employer must take the person on by written law`)
    AND (NOT `the hiring`'s `the employer must take the person on by a pre-1971 agreement`)

GIVEN `the hiring` IS A Hiring
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the hiring contravenes the order` IF
        `the order applies to the hiring` `the hiring`
    AND (NOT `the hiring`'s `the person is a registered person`)
    AND (NOT `the hiring`'s `the Director consented in writing`)

§§ `5(4), (5) -- the employer's fine, and the employee's contract`

-- s 5(4): an employer who contravenes an order "shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $2,000, and in respect of each
-- employee employed by him in contravention of any such provision, to a further fine not exceeding $50 for every day on which that
-- employee is so employed". No imprisonment.
-- `employee-days` is the sum, over every employee wrongly employed, of the days each was so employed.
GIVEN `employee-days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for contravening an order` MEANS 2000 PLUS 50 TIMES `employee-days`

-- s 5(5): the person employed "shall not, by reason only of that contravention, be deemed to be employed under an illegal contract of
-- employment".
GIVEN `the hiring` IS A Hiring
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract is illegal by reason only of the order` IF FALSE

§§ `6 -- consent, refusal and appeal`

-- s 6(1): an employer bound by an order who "is unable to find a registered person whom he considers suitable to fill any vacancy" may,
-- after obtaining the written consent of the Director, employ any other person.
-- (2): if the Director refuses, he "shall notify the employer in writing of the refusal and his reasons", and a dissatisfied employer
-- "may, within 14 days of the refusal, appeal to the Appeals Board".
-- (4): the Board's decision "shall be final and conclusive and shall not be called in question in any court".
-- How the 14 days are counted is not in the Act; the count here is calendar days after the refusal (an inference).
GIVEN `the Director refused consent` IS A BOOLEAN, `days since the refusal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer may appeal to the Appeals Board` IF
    `the Director refused consent` AND `days since the refusal` AT MOST 14

GIVEN `the Appeals Board has decided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision may be challenged in court` IF FALSE

§§ `7 -- the registered person must report a new job`

-- s 7(1): "Any registered person shall, upon securing employment, notify the Director in writing within 7 days of the employment."
-- (2): "Any person who fails to comply with subsection (1) shall have his name deleted from the register."
-- The only consequence the Act states is deletion. There is no fine, and s 7 creates no offence.
GIVEN `is registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `has secured employment` IS A BOOLEAN, `notified in writing` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days taken to notify` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the name is to be deleted from the register` IF
        `is registered`
    AND `has secured employment`
    AND (    (NOT `notified in writing`)
         OR  `days taken to notify` GREATER THAN 7)

§§ `8 -- entry and requests for information`

-- s 8(1)(a): the Director or an authorised public officer may, "on producing, if so required, documentary evidence of his identity",
-- "enter, at any reasonable time, any premises other than premises used solely as a dwelling".
GIVEN `at a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN, `the premises are used solely as a dwelling` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `identity was asked for` IS A BOOLEAN, `identity was produced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may enter` IF
        `at a reasonable time`
    AND (NOT `the premises are used solely as a dwelling`)
    AND ((NOT `identity was asked for`) OR `identity was produced`)

-- s 8(2): an offence to "(a) wilfully obstruct" the officer; "(b) fail to produce or furnish any document or information in accordance
-- with a request"; or "(c) knowingly make any false statement for any purpose connected with this Act".
GIVEN `wilfully obstructed the officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `failed to produce what was requested` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knowingly made a false statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 8 is committed` IF
        `wilfully obstructed the officer`
    OR  `failed to produce what was requested`
    OR  `knowingly made a false statement`

§§ `9 -- summons`

-- s 9(1): the person summoned "shall attend at the time and place specified in the summons and answer truthfully all questions".
-- (2): only one who "neglects to attend as required by the summons" commits the s 9 offence. An untrue answer is not an offence under
-- s 9 itself; a knowingly false statement is caught by s 8(2)(c).
GIVEN `was summoned` IS A BOOLEAN, `attended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 9 is committed` IF `was summoned` AND (NOT `attended`)

§§ `5(4), 8(2), 9(2) -- maximum penalties`

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `contravening an order under section 5`
    `obstruction, non-production or false statement under section 8`
    `neglecting a summons under section 9`

-- The base fine only; s 5(4) adds $50 per employee per day (see above).
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum base fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `contravening an order under section 5` THEN 2000
    WHEN `obstruction, non-production or false statement under section 8` THEN 1000
    WHEN `neglecting a summons under section 9` THEN 500

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `contravening an order under section 5` THEN 0
    WHEN `obstruction, non-production or false statement under section 8` THEN 6
    WHEN `neglecting a summons under section 9` THEN 3

§§ `10 -- officers of a body corporate`

-- s 10: where an offence by a body corporate "is proved to have been committed with the consent or connivance of, or to be
-- attributable to any reckless neglect of duty on the part of, any director, manager, secretary or other officer", that officer "as
-- well as the body corporate shall be guilty of that offence".
GIVEN `the body corporate committed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a director, manager, secretary or other officer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `consented or connived` IS A BOOLEAN, `reckless neglect of duty is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is also guilty` IF
        `the body corporate committed an offence`
    AND `is a director, manager, secretary or other officer`
    AND (`consented or connived` OR `reckless neglect of duty is proved`)
